sxml-qt4 run - Run test cases and check their assertions

Usage: sxml-qt4 run [--catalog=FILE] [--spec=SPEC] [--test-set=NAME] [--format=FORMAT] [TEST-LIST]

Runs each selected test case with its environment (sources,
parameters, namespaces, static base URI, decimal formats, the
default collation, resources, collections) in a processor of its own,
with at most 10^8 evaluation steps and 512 MiB, and checks its
result assertions. Writes each test case that failed, ended in
error or raised a wrong error code, then counts per test set and
a "total:" line; --format=json writes every test case, counts
per test set and per area, and how many are in the D95 scope. The
selection is the test cases of TEST-LIST, those of the test set
--test-set names, or with neither every test case of the catalog.
Exits 1 when a test case failed or ended in error, 3 when a file
cannot be read.

Options:
  -h, --help           Show this help and exit
      --catalog=FILE   The catalog.xml of the suite (default: third_party/qt4tests/catalog.xml)
      --spec=SPEC      The language and version the run targets (one of: XP40, XQ40; default: XP40)
      --test-set=NAME  Run every test case of one test set
      --format=FORMAT  The form of the report (one of: text, json; default: text)

Arguments:
  TEST-LIST  File naming test cases, one '<test-set> <test-case>' per line

Examples:
  sxml-qt4 run tests/qt4/torture-slice.txt
  sxml-qt4 run --test-set=fn-abs
  sxml-qt4 run --format=json > report.json
